Article 19
(1) In the framework of providing protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government establishes UPTDPPA.
(2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services for:
a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organization and work procedures of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by a Regent Regulation.
